"""Pass 13: misconception tags for every chapter-check objective that had none (50 objectives: ITSUP 2.1–13.3,
NETOPS 1.1–9.2). Same rules as pass 11 (curriculum_v2/misconceptions.py): a distractor is tagged only when the
wrong idea it represents is clear from the item, its key and its explanation; throw-away distractors stay
untagged; labels describe the wrong belief and add no new curriculum facts; the corrective text a student sees
is assembled from existing lesson sections. Written by Grok Bot from the items; pending SME review like the rest."""


def _m(obj, label, fix, terms):
    return {'obj': obj, 'label': label, 'fix': fix, 'terms': terms}


